# Go testing

Tests are required for changed behavior. Use the standard `testing` package and table-driven cases (`t.Run` per case).

From `apps/api`:

```bash
go test ./...
```

Run `go test -race ./...` when the change touches shared state (goroutines, pools, caches, locks). There is no numeric coverage target. CI publishes a coverage artifact with no gate.

Live PostgreSQL tests stay skipped unless `TEST_DATABASE_URL` or `DATABASE_URL` is set. `config.Load` and `cmd/*` need `JOB_BINDING_SECRET` and `SCRIPT_SIGNING_KEY` (32-byte base64 or 64 hex). Logs and `t.Fatal` / `t.Error` text must not echo those values or any other secret.
